GROWTH GAPS

1. Challenge-Based Storytelling vs. Tool Listing
Top-performing creators like @dhavalkataria_ (20.47% engagement) structure their videos around high-stakes challenges and narrative arcs (e.g., "Can I make 50,000 INR using Raj Shamani's business idea? Episode 1 of UN-BROKE-ING INDIA") or bold contrarian statements. In contrast, @garvit.irl primarily uses feature listings and tool comparisons (Dots vs. Muse vs. Grokbot). While informative, tool reviews lack emotional stakes, capping shareability and mass-market reach.

2. GitHub Social Proof and Zero-Cost Authority Hooks
Creators like @nick_saraev (7815.3 avg likes) and @thevarunmayya (23312.5 avg likes) capture outsized reach by attaching quantitative social proof to open-source software (e.g., "agency inside Claude Code for 0 dollars", "already crossed 160k stars on GitHub", "REA crossed 130,000 stars"). While @garvit.irl covers open-source voice cloning and Claude skills, the scripts lack clear social proof metrics (GitHub stars, benchmark stats, enterprise cost comparisons) that validate the tool's authority within the first 3 seconds.

3. Static Post Drag vs. Reel Dominance
Data shows @garvit.irl averages 201 likes on Reels across 16 posts, but drops to just 31 likes on static posts across 4 posts. Every top competitor in this cohort generates their viral volume exclusively through Reels with dynamic screen recordings, physical gestures, and fast pacing. Spending production time on static posts dilutes algorithmic momentum and suppresses aggregate reach.


RECOMMENDED ACTIONS

1. Eliminate Static Posts and Shift 100% to Reels (6:00 PM - 9:00 PM IST)
Cease all single-image and carousel static posts immediately. Dedicate all bandwidth to 3 to 4 Reels per week scheduled strictly inside the verified peak window of 6:00 PM to 9:00 PM IST, where your audience is most active and conversion to engagement is highest.

2. Introduce a "Build in Public / Challenge" Series
Replicate the serialized framework utilized by @dhavalkataria_ by launching a dedicated series (e.g., "Replacing a 50,000 INR Agency with Open-Source AI: Day 1"). Shift the narrative from "here is a tool" to "watch me solve a real business problem step-by-step using this tool."

3. Anchor Hooks with Quantitative Authority and GitHub Metrics
Revamp the first 3 seconds of technical Reels to incorporate external social proof rather than generic software comparisons. Structure the visual and verbal hook around metrics: mention the number of GitHub stars, the exact cost savings in thousands of rupees, or how many developers use it before walking through the deployment tutorial. Double down on comment-trigger automation ("Comment REPO to get the direct GitHub link and prompt template") to preserve your 128.4 median comment volume.
